From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:19:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/24] Test durable and opted-out commits on logs that cannot
 sync (#2818)

Issue2818_FlushFallback_Tests and Issue2818_DurableCommits_Tests: the
old degraded-path coverage (a rejected device sync degrades commits and
checkpoints to OS-cache flushes) moves to "durable commits=false"
(proposed default A). With durable commits a log that stops syncing
after the proof fails its commit with an unknown outcome (note 4), an
explicit checkpoint on such a log throws before it overwrites data
(note 5), and a failed checkpoint sync no longer closes the engine for
reads: each asserts exact rows, unchanged files, $database.writeFailure
and the refused next write (decision 6). The log-sync checkpoint tests
move to a partial file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
